      "pins": ["J1.20", "J1.24", "J2.20", "J2.24", "R11.2"],
      "nets": ["/PIN24"],
      "observed": "Net /PIN24 connects J1 pin 20, J1 pin 24, J2 pin 20, J2 pin 24, and R11 pin 2, shorting M5Stack bus pins 20 and 24 together on both connectors.",
      "expected": "Pin 20 should connect only to R11.2 for PWM2 selection (per spec, R11 selects bus pin 20), and pin 24 should be an independent pass-through net between J1.24 and J2.24. They must not be tied together.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"15\") (name \"/PIN24\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"J1\") (pin \"20\") (pinfunction \"Pin_20\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"J1\") (pin \"24\") (pinfunction \"Pin_24\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"J2\") (pin \"20\") (pinfunction \"Pin_20\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"J2\") (pin \"24\") (pinfunction \"Pin_24\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"R11\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R9–R12 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | Select which M5Stack bus pin (pin 19/21 for ch.1, pin 20/22 for ch.2) supplies PWM1/PWM2"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Shorting two independent M5Stack bus GPIOs together can cause contention, malfunction, or damage if either pin is driven by the M5Stack or a stacked module.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a bridged-net anomaly: M5Stack bus pin 20 and pin 24 are shorted together on both connectors (J1 and J2), which is not intended by the specification."
}

